From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Don't audit vendor_init reading
 vts.native_server.on

Samsung's init.vendor.rilcommon.rc (a blob) has

  on property:vts.native_server.on=*
      setprop vendor.vts.native_server.on ${vts.native_server.on}

When init parses vendor rc files it checks that the vendor_init
subcontext may read every property trigger (CanReadProperty in
property_service.cpp); vts.native_server.on is vts_status_prop, a
system_restricted_prop vendor_init has no get_prop for, so the action
is rejected with "ParseTriggers() failed: unexported property trigger
found: vts.native_server.on" and this is logged at every boot:

  avc: denied { read } for property=vts.native_server.on pid=0 uid=0 gid=0
  scontext=u:r:vendor_init:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:vts_status_prop:s0
  tclass=file permissive=0

vts.native_server.on is only ever set by the VTS test harness (it stops
audioserver & co. for native-server tests), so the mirrored vendor
property has no use on a shipping build. Silence it like the existing
radio_prop/system_prop dontaudits in this file rather than granting the
read; the init parse message stays, by design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/vendor_init.te | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/vendor_init.te b/sepolicy/vendor/vendor_init.te
index 2d5d744..4205aed 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/vendor_init.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/vendor_init.te
@@ -14,3 +14,5 @@ allow vendor_init sysfs_graphics_writable:file rw_file_perms;
 
 dontaudit vendor_init radio_prop:file read;
 dontaudit vendor_init system_prop:file read;
+# on property:vts.native_server.on=* in Samsung's init.vendor.rilcommon.rc
+dontaudit vendor_init vts_status_prop:file read;
